<main class="commercial" id="main-content"><div class="wrap">
<section class="cr-hero" aria-labelledby="cr-headline"><div class="cr-hero-copy"><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO · Head & Neck · Kyrgyzstan</p><h1 id="cr-headline">Persistent neck tension?</h1><p class="cr-lead">CRANIO provides percussion-assisted soft-tissue sessions for the upper neck and occipital muscles. We compare comfort and movement before and after. This is not medical treatment.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="https://wa.me/996998066098?text=Hello!%20I%20would%20like%20to%20ask%20about%20a%20CRANIO%20session%3A%20location%2C%20fees%20and%20available%20times." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-booking="whatsapp">Book via WhatsApp</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="#session">How a session works</a></div><p class="cr-small">This practice is not medical diagnosis or treatment. Individual outcomes vary and are not guaranteed.</p></div><aside class="cr-process" aria-label="What happens at an appointment"><p class="cr-kicker">01 / 04</p><h2>What happens at an appointment</h2><ol><li>Discuss your concern and relevant limitations</li><li>Check movement, sensations and observable reference points</li><li>Work with soft tissues in the head and neck region</li><li>Compare observations afterward and discuss next steps</li></ol><p class="cr-small">You do not need to buy a device; the practitioner uses the instrument during the session.</p></aside></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="concerns"><p class="cr-kicker">Start with what feels familiar</p><h2>Reasons people contact us</h2><p class="cr-intro">The same symptom can have different causes. Head position alone cannot establish a diagnosis, and we do not promise to resolve every problem.</p><div class="cr-concerns"><a class="cr-concern" href="experience/neck-tension/"><span>01</span>Persistent neck tension<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="experience/neck-stiffness/"><span>02</span>Neck stiffness and limited motion<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="experience/screen-work/"><span>03</span>Screen-related fatigue<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="experience/head-tension/"><span>04</span>Tension around the back of the head<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="experience/facial-asymmetry/"><span>05</span>Facial and jaw asymmetry<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="experience/comfortable-head/"><span>06</span>Difficulty finding a comfortable head position<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="session"><p class="cr-kicker">A practical explanation</p><h2>What to expect at a first visit</h2><p class="cr-intro">We start with conversation and observation, then practical work if there is no reason to recommend medical assessment or to avoid the session.</p><div class="cr-steps"><div class="cr-card"><h3>01 · Conversation</h3><p>What you notice, how long it has been present, relevant assessments and warning signs.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>02 · Initial observations</h3><p>Comfort, movement and — with consent — standardized photographs, when appropriate.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>03 · Practical session</h3><p>A practitioner applies percussion-assisted soft-tissue work to the upper neck and occipital muscles, adjusting intensity to the individual.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>04 · Reassessment</h3><p>We compare observations, including when nothing changes, and consider whether further visits make sense.</p></div></div><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="how-it-works/">How a session works ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="results"><p class="cr-kicker">Observations, not promises</p><h2>What we pay attention to</h2><p class="cr-intro">The practitioner has reported individual changes in perceived neck tension, freedom of movement and visible symmetry. These reports do not establish treatment efficacy.</p><div class="cr-three"><div class="cr-card"><h3>Movement</h3><p>Turning and tilting the head; any limitation and sense of effort.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Experience</h3><p>Perceived tension, head comfort and how you feel before and after.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Symmetry</h3><p>Comparable photos, with informed consent, consistent angle and lighting.</p></div></div><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="cases/">How case records are documented ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section cr-split" id="model"><div><p class="cr-kicker">The C0–C1 model</p><h2>Why the occipital region matters in this approach</h2></div><div><p>C0 refers to the occipital bone, and C1 to the first cervical vertebra (atlas). CRANIO explores a hypothesis that relative skull position and muscular adaptation in this region could contribute to some movement and postural compensation patterns.</p><p class="cr-small cr-hypothesis">This is a research hypothesis, not an established explanation for all asymmetry, headaches or other conditions. External observation cannot establish bone displacement.</p><a class="cr-text-link" href="c0-c1/">Explore the C0–C1 model ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="pricing"><p class="cr-kicker">Clear terms before you visit</p><h2>Sessions and indicative fees</h2><p class="cr-intro">Indicative prices from the previously defined Kyrgyzstan program. Please confirm current fees, location and availability in WhatsApp.</p><div class="cr-prices"><div><span>Initial session</span><strong>15 000 <small>KGS</small></strong></div><div><span>Follow-up session</span><strong>8 000 <small>KGS</small></strong></div><div><span>Three-session program</span><strong>31 000 <small>KGS</small></strong></div></div><p class="cr-small">Further sessions are not mandatory; their relevance is discussed after the first visit. Payments and terms are agreed directly with the practitioner.</p></section>
<section class="cr-section cr-split" id="author"><div><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS</p><h2>Who is behind CRANIO</h2></div><div><p>CRANIO SYSTEMS is an author-developed practical approach and research model by Lian Axis, informed by years of personal observations of head and neck work. Describing this experience is not a clinical efficacy claim.</p><a class="cr-text-link" href="method/">Read about the method ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section cr-safety" id="safety" role="note"><div><h2>When to seek medical care first</h2><p>Sudden severe headache, numbness or weakness, speech or vision changes, or pain after a head or neck injury require urgent medical assessment. Do not substitute a nonmedical session for necessary care.</p></div><p class="cr-small">CRANIO is a nonmedical soft-tissue practice and self-observation framework, not diagnosis or treatment.</p></section>
<section class="cr-section"><h2>Quick answers</h2><div class="cr-faq"><details><summary>Do I need to buy a device?</summary><p>No. The practitioner uses the percussion tool during a session.</p></details><details><summary>Will my atlas be adjusted?</summary><p>No cervical manipulation or vertebral adjustment is claimed. Work focuses on soft tissue, and external observation alone cannot verify bone alignment.</p></details><details><summary>Will one session fix the problem?</summary><p>No results are guaranteed. We document what changes and what does not. Discuss medical symptoms with a clinician.</p></details><details><summary>What is TwinMind?</summary><p>An optional concept for continuity of observation records. No app or account is required for a session.</p></details></div></section>
<section class="cr-finale" id="contact"><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS · +996 998 066 098</p><h2>Tell us what is bothering you</h2><p>Message us about your head or neck concern and ask about appointment format, location and available times.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="https://wa.me/996998066098?text=Hello!%20I%20would%20like%20to%20ask%20about%20a%20CRANIO%20session%3A%20location%2C%20fees%20and%20available%20times." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-booking="whatsapp">Ask about an appointment</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="primordocciput/">Research and development history ↗</a></div></section></div></main>